-- Issue 138: the contents of a CONTAINING are encoded by the referenced type assignment's own functions, also when it
-- shares the typedef of another type: an alias with an ACN specification of its own (`Sub ::= T`, `Sub [size 24]`)
-- and a WITH COMPONENTS subtype (`WSub ::= TR (WITH COMPONENTS ...)`, which takes no ACN specification from TR: its
-- r has the default 16 bits, not TR's 32) share `typedef T` / `typedef TR`. Before, the call and its buffer were
-- named after the typedef (T, TR) while the region's sizes were the referenced type's: --acn-v2 wrote T's encoding
-- into Sub's region (Q12 05 05 80 instead of 00 00 05 00 00 05 80), legacy rejected the sites. Legacy and --acn-v2.
-- No directives: run by v4Tests/scripts/runWireTests.sh with 014_wire_test.c / 014_wire_test.adb.
ACN-WIRE-CALLEE DEFINITIONS AUTOMATIC TAGS ::= BEGIN
    T     ::= INTEGER (0..255)
    Sub   ::= T
    Q12   ::= SEQUENCE { f OCTET STRING (CONTAINING Sub), g BIT STRING (CONTAINING Sub), z BOOLEAN }
    TR    ::= SEQUENCE { r INTEGER (0..65535), k INTEGER (0..7) }
    WSub  ::= TR (WITH COMPONENTS {..., k (0..3)})
    Q9    ::= SEQUENCE { f OCTET STRING (CONTAINING WSub), z BOOLEAN }
END
